<title>UK: SEK sets 10 billion yen dual currency (NZ$) bond.</title>
<headline>SEK sets 10 billion yen dual currency (NZ$) bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following dual currency bond was announced by sole manager Kokusai Europe Ltd.</p>
<p> BORROWER   SWEDISH EXPORT CREDIT CORP</p>
<p> AMT    *10 BLN YEN   COUPON     6.10	MATURITY    28.JAN.99</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE    28.JAN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  =	   LISTING    NONE	PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  =	   DENOMS (M) 1	 SALE LIMITS US/UK/JP/NZ</p>
<p> NOTES     *REDEMPTION IN NZ$ AT 1.0 MLN YEN = NZ$12,106.53</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
